WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.780
Good morning, John!

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.440
I spent a bunch of time at the DFTVA.com Warehouse this week,

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:05.560
because it's gettin' into the busy season!

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.700
Not that they don't have it handled.

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.040
I mostly just sign.. stuff.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:09.020
It is a really big place,

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.660
filled with a bunch of really cool stuff!

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.300
We work with a ton of amazing creators now:

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:12.880
Hannah Hart,

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:13.620
and Rhett and Link,

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.780
and Glozell Green,

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:15.640
and MinuteEarth,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:16.980
and This Star Won't Go Out.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:17.640
We sell shirts,

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.160
and hats,

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:18.720
and posters,

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:19.300
and mugs,

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.160
and tea...

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.720
And, I'm just happy that we get to send people stuff that they like;

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:26.040
and help creative people do what they want to do for a living.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:26.640
And today,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.720
the day after Thanksgiving,

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.620
I'm actually recording this on Thanksgiving.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.680
And also, the day after, John,

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:34.440
you made a video about how we are apparently incapable of understanding how

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.140
good the world is, comparatively.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.080
I gotta say!

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.440
Sometimes, it is hard

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:40.700
to keep in mind,

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.460
how..

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.920
nice your life is.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:43.860
Like, thought experiment here:

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.920
say we cure cancer..

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:45.760
tomorrow.

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:46.720
Mass celebrations!

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:47.220
Right?

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.440
Like, people would not be able to stop smiling

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:50.260
for days.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:50.960
And, for years,

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:53.860
we would continue feeling the amazingness of that achievement.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.160
But, twenty or thirty years later,

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.980
we would still know that it was great;

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.680
there would be less suffering in the world,

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:00.660
less death.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.860
But, we would normalize;

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.660
we'd just live in a world without cancer.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.640
How do I know this, for sure?

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.100
Well, it's happened before;

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.420
I mean, we used to not have antibiotics and vaccines.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.960
Those things have saved billions-

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:12.600
BILLIONS of lives;

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.780
and yet, we go on everyday just sort of thinking:

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:15.400
"Yeah, you know,

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.260
antibiotics and vaccines.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:17.860
They're nice."

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.060
But, we aren't deeply and emotionally touched

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.760
by the magnificent,

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:22.480
magic

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.880
that is this ability

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.040
to not die;

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.440
the way that humans always used to die!

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.220
Another example:

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.220
uh- I was born into an America

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:30.720
where

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.100
two people could be denied the right to marry,

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.120
because of their gender.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.240
And, so was everyone else watching this video,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.100
unless you are less than 6 months old;

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:38.640
in which case,

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.900
glpblpblpdpbpgp

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:40.600
bgaaaw!!

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.460
But, we've already stopped being excited about that!

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:43.660
And, maybe that's GOOD!!

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.660
That we're not designed to say,

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.660
"Well, I guess we've done pretty well.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.760
Might as well stop progressing..."

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:50.460
Objectively,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:53.420
on average, this is the best time to be alive in human history.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.260
I mean, I know I say that as someone who,

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.820
like, literally wearing-

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.220
like, the most-

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.620
preppy thing I've ever worn on VlogBrothers!

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.460
It's Thanksgiving!

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:02.160
I'm dressed up.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.160
We have achieved

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.560
so much to decrease the suffering of people!!

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.560
During my Grandmother's life,

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.320
there was a war in which 60 million people died.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.100
60

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:10.700
million!

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.500
My Mother was born into an America

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.500
where black people had different schools,

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.800
and different bathrooms!

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.500
But, it's impossible to go through life feeling all of these accomplishments every second;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.580
and, maybe we shouldn't!

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.560
Maybe it's beautiful

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.220
that we move on from our successes

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.540
and immediately fret over the next giant,

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.760
magnificent problem that we have to overcome.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.060
But, if we never look back,

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:30.840
and never think about what we've done;

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.020
then it all looks hopeless.

00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:33.120
It looks impossible!

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.300
Which is why it has to be a mix

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.860
of- of dissatisfaction with the way that it is,

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.160
and what could be better,

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.520
and we have to work for that;

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:43.580
and also recognizing that we've done a great deal of remarkable things,

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.540
as a species, and as individuals.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:47.740
Like, I get to live in a world without smallpox;

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:51.380
and in a world with twenty one pilots songs and pumpkin pie.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.060
One day a year of Thanksgiving,

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:54.600
is not enough days of the year.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.100
This is something that I think

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.520
really is powerful,

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:58.700
and motivates me,

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.120
and makes me happier and more effective!

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.140
Just to be thankful

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.200
for the literal billions of people,

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.480
who have worked hard to make life better for their children;

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:08.040
ah, euh-

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.640
because I'm one of those children!

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:10.140
And I hope

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.680
that I can honour the memory of those people;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:13.680
by both appreciating what they've done,

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:14.980
and also building on it.

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:15.780
John,

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.820
I'll see you on Tuesday.

